  "worked_solution": "Let's draw our vertical arrow through the given region. The arrow should be pointing away from the axis of rotation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14222582/assets/d5593e8c1e1d544acb8824d9428823d3d6cef3971a1cedd4b087a7902b0e2239.png)\n\nThe vertical arrow \n\n- *enters* the region through the inner curve $y=3-3{x}^{2},$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the outer curve $y=2{x}^{2}-2x.$\n\nNow, we can find the volume of our solid as the difference between the volumes of the solids generated by the outer and inner curves.\n\n- **Step I.** Figure out the volume generated by the outer curve $y=2{x}^{2}-2x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14222582/assets/bddc78f683e28ec6e97fddb32f95dfdaaff27d3aafbdfc61f424857916f81a6c.png)\n\nThe corresponding volume is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{\\text{outer}} & =\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}[\\,(\\text{upper})-(\\text{lower})\\,]^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}[\\,(5)-(2{x}^{2}-2x)\\,]^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}{[5-2{x}^{2}+2x]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step II.** Figure out the volume generated by the inner curve $y=3-3{x}^{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14222582/assets/cc049c46593baf1d96c04b95680d6b444ab9ceffc64d1f23f310f70e78684c14.png)\n\nThe corresponding volume is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{\\text{inner}} & =\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}[\\,(\\text{upper})-(\\text{lower})\\,]^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}[\\,(5)-(3-3{x}^{2})\\,]^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}{[2+3{x}^{2}]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step III.** Find the difference.\n\nFinally, we can write the volume of the original solid as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={V}_{\\text{outer}}-{V}_{\\text{inner}} \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}{[5-2{x}^{2}+2x]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}{[2+3{x}^{2}]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{-3/5}^{1}({[5-2{x}^{2}+2x]}^{2}-{[2+3{x}^{2}]}^{2})\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
